module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.identity_cast_compares_type_spellings

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { NoRungStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.
data identity_cast_compares_type_spellings: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "identity_cast_compares_type_spellings" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an identity-cast decision compares source and target type spellings instead of their resolved identities. A qualified inferred name and a bare target spelling can therefore disagree even when both denote the same carrier. HARM: accepted source fails during execution on an unnecessary identity conversion, inviting authors to normalize spellings locally and leave the decision broken.",
    "SPECIMEN, gunbc#11182 on 2026-09-12: the scoped Spark claim_batch run accepted empty_map() as Map<InventoryLotIdentity, Nat> and then refused with cannot cast std.types.Map (runtime carrier Map) to Map. v1_interpreter cast_identity_result compares source_name == target_name; eval_cast has numeric conversion and string cases but no map conversion. The runtime failure occurred at initialization before the typed-map lookup ran. The inventory row now initializes its already-typed map field directly with empty_map(), following existing map construction rather than requesting a conversion; this removes a redundant operation and does not repair cast identity.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: source and target must resolve to the same type with the same arguments; equal carrier labels alone are not sufficient, since distinct brands or parameterizations may require refusal. Compare a qualified/bare identity pair with a genuinely different target as the discriminating control. This differs from carrier_by_spelling, where a bare import selects a different declaration: here the failed decision never compares resolved declarations.",
    "FOUND AT MITIGATABLE through a located runtime type-error, not a compile-time guarantee. CEILING: STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED for resolved type identity, which is decidable. NEXT TRIGGER: identity casts use resolved type identities and arguments across qualified, bare and alias presentations, while nonidentity conversions retain their modeled admission/refusal rules. Normalizing one Map spelling or deleting this specimen's cast does not discharge that capability.",
    "SPECIMEN ON THE EMISSION PATH, 2026-10-25 (quiet-bear-692): `name as String` for name: extdeps.git GitRemoteName (an alias of NonEmptyStr) in git_remote_url_config_key was emitted by v1.compiler.emit emit_typed_cast_shared as panic!(\"unsupported cast from GitRemoteName to String\") with no blocking diagnostic. The decision compared the rendered alias spelling against `String`, and its representation walk followed only the reference's own resolved node, so it stopped at the alias declaration; its fallback compared realization rows by dag_name, then occurrence identity. REPAIR: cast_representation_identical walks each side through its DECLARED transparent edges -- the alias right-hand side (v1.compiler.infer_env alias_rhs_of_declaration) and the where-refinement base -- reading each edge from the declaration the position resolves to (type_reference_declaration_reading, with lookup_type_for for a position the reading cannot place), and compares the kernel mint or declaration reached. The grounded-natural sibling (std.nat Nat as Int, the same misread by rendered spelling) is read from the grounding rows by cast_source_grounded_onto_target_carrier (#14769). Controls: test.claim.emitter_nested_refinement_cast_witness alias_of_refinement_cast_emits_the_operand (the extdeps.git specimen plus a local alias), with unrelated_carriers_still_refuse_the_cast as the red. A cast no carrier, crossing or cast rule answers still emits a runtime abort; its compile-time refusal is the stacked follow-up change. RUNG UNCHANGED for the class as a whole: the interpreter's cast identity (the first specimen) is not touched.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
